Description: scrollable, man-page-styled Linux CPU usage monitor
 cpumon reads /proc/stat (aggregate and per-core user/nice/system/idle/
 iowait/irq/softirq/steal jiffie counters, context switches, forks,
 running/blocked process counts) along with /proc/loadavg, /proc/uptime,
 and /proc/cpuinfo, and displays it as a scrollable, man-page-styled
 terminal report that auto-refreshes on a configurable interval (seconds,
 minutes, hours, or days).
 .
 It also runs headless via a bundled systemd service (enabled and started
 automatically on install), appending timestamped snapshots to a daily
 log file. Log files are pruned automatically after a configurable
 retention period (30 days by default; see /etc/cpumon/cpumon.conf).

